throws keyword used when we did not want to handle exception in method rather than managing it in main method where we use try catch block to run that method 




class Main {
    
    public void divide(int i) throws ArithmeticException{
        System.out.println(5/i);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
       
       Main obj=new Main();
       
       try{
           obj.divide(0);
       }
       
       catch(Exception e){
           System.out.println(e);
       }
       
    }
}





